{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"optimistic-state-drops-at-settlement","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optimistic state drops at settlement"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pre-repair executable revision: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"origin/main"},{"type":"text","value":" at "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"95c3f9ec9"},{"type":"text","value":".\nRepair branch: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fix-settled-snapshot-ack"},{"type":"text","value":". Production code "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"b5e498ddb"},{"type":"text","value":"\nthrough "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"9b82ac3dc"},{"type":"text","value":". Evidence head "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"3c85ac0de"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"law","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Law"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An optimistic transaction overlays its optimistic state only while its\nmutation function runs. When the mutation function settles, fulfilled or\nrejected, the state drops. Success does not wait for a sync confirmation: a\nhandler that returns before its server row arrives shows the previous synced\nrow until that row applies."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A sync transaction committed while an optimistic transaction persists is\n"},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"accepted"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and held. It becomes "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"visible"}]},{"type":"text","value":" in the publication that drops the\noptimistic state, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isPersisted"},{"type":"text","value":" settles after that publication."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each sync transaction therefore has two moments:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Accepted:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"commit()"},{"type":"text","value":" returns, or a persistence wrapper finishes its\ndurable step. Handler-facing writes wait for this moment: Query Collection\ndirect writes, persisted mutation confirmation and startup, and the PowerSync\nmutation path."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Visible:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" the rows apply and publish. Commit receipts, subset loads, and\nCollection readiness wait for this moment."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An accepted transaction always applies, in commit order, and a later abort\ncannot withdraw its rows. A load whose caller aborted still rejects with\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AbortError"},{"type":"text","value":". A source discards a stale page by checking the signal before\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"commit()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A sync write is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"$origin: 'local'"},{"type":"text","value":" only if it was committed while the\ntransaction persisted. A write committed after settlement is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'remote'"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Authority: user decisions recorded in the PR discussion for this branch. These\nreplace the accepted-snapshot retention law (#1213, #1807, #1822, #1870) and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"begin({ immediate })"},{"type":"text","value":" (#1130)."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"gap","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Gap"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Since #1213, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recomputeOptimisticState"},{"type":"text","value":" retained a completed direct\ntransaction's row until a later sync transaction wrote its key. Query\nCollection direct writes used "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"begin({ immediate: true })"},{"type":"text","value":" to apply during\npersistence. After such a write, no later sync transaction retired the\nretained row. Passing runs of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"awaits persisted server responses in update handlers"},{"type":"text","value":" depended on an unrelated persisted sync transaction arriving later."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The optimistic-history oracle encoded the retention law as its reference\nmodel, so the oracle agreed with the drift."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In #1990, a refetch canceled an earlier result's commit that was waiting for\nstorage. The cancellation invalidated the dependent result, and the collection\nentered "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"error"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"repair-and-witnesses","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Repair and witnesses"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Core:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" removes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"begin({ immediate })"},{"type":"text","value":", post-commit cancellation, retention\nand its dependency machinery, the truncate optimistic snapshot, and the\ndirect-transaction marker. The only hold left keeps a completed row while a\nqueued sync transaction touches its key."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Receipts:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" a commit receipt resolves at visibility. It carries its\nacceptance moment ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withAcceptedReceipt"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"whenSyncAccepted"},{"type":"text","value":"). Readiness\nwaits for accepted rows to publish."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Query Collection:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" direct writes read and validate accepted rows, and\nupdate the Query cache after acceptance. That cache read was the root cause\nof #1130. A refetch commits without a signal and no longer rolls back\naccepted ownership. An eager fetch that started before a direct write is\ndiscarded."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Persistence:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" stores a held source transaction at acceptance. Internal\napplies inside the apply mutex wait only for acceptance. Electric reserves\nits commit turn through "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"persistence.reserveCommitTurn()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Electric and TrailBase:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" reject an aborted load after its accepted rows\napply."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optimistic-history oracle:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" the prose, model, grammar, and driver are\nrewritten. The handler writes at every cut, with and without awaiting\nacceptance. It observes the rows visible when "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isPersisted"},{"type":"text","value":" settles, allows a\nsingle cut at settlement, keeps receipts pending while queued, and checks\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"$origin"},{"type":"text","value":" for held and later confirmations."}]}]}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Run"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Result"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"#1990 refetch, first durable write held, on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"origin/main"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"3 of 3 isolated runs fail: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"expected 'error' to be 'ready'"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"#1990 handler "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"writeUpsert"},{"type":"text","value":", result write held, on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"origin/main"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"4 of 5 full-file runs fail: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"expected +0 to be 3"},{"type":"text","value":" (the retained optimistic row)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Real-SQLite handler test ported from #2002, on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"origin/main"},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"await source.commit()"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"times out after 5000 ms"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Same three on the branch"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"pass; Query Collection file passes 5 of 5 full-file runs"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"awaits persisted server responses in update handlers"},{"type":"text","value":", branch"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"20 of 20 full-file runs pass"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Eager refetch older than a handler "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"writeUpsert"},{"type":"text","value":", before its fix"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"expected 2 to be 3"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"mutants","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mutants"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each mutant is a temporary production edit that is restored after its run."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mutant"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Owner"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Result"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Retention kept: hold a completed row without a queued sync transaction"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"state-retention oracle"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"killed"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Held sync applies before the drop (immediate bypass)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"state-retention oracle"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"killed, 11 failures"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isPersisted"},{"type":"text","value":" resolves before publication"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"state-retention oracle"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"killed, 40 failures"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Handler-facing receipt waits for visibility"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"state-retention oracle"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"killed, 6 failures"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Load settles at acceptance"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"load-subset oracle and state retention"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"killed, 10 and 4 failures"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"$origin"},{"type":"text","value":" marker persists until the next write"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"state-retention oracle"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"killed, 6 failures"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Held confirmation marked "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'remote'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"state-retention oracle"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"killed, 7 failures"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Core abort cancels an accepted transaction"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"load-subset and refinement oracles"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"killed"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stale eager fetch applies"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Query Collection"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"killed"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Query cache reads applied rows"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Query Collection"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"killed"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TrailBase aborted load resolves"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TrailBase"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"killed"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Electric aborted load resolves"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Electric"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"killed"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Query Collection passes its signal to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"commit()"},{"type":"text","value":" again"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Query Collection"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"survived; equivalent"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Query Collection rolls back accepted ownership on supersession"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ownership oracle"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"survived at first, then killed"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Survivors:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Signal passed to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"commit()"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"text","value":" this mutant is equivalent. Core now ignores\na post-commit abort, so the signal cannot cancel an accepted transaction. The\ncore-level mutant above covers this law."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ownership rollback:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" every supersession test held durable storage. In that\ncase the result's core transaction had already applied, so restoring the old\nownership did nothing. The ownership oracle now also holds the result behind\na persisting mutation and checks visible and synced rows after each refetch,\nincluding a later empty refetch. The mutant fails there."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"after-the-merge-with-the-state-stack-refactor","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After the merge with the state-stack refactor"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every mutant above, plus five more, ran again on the merged code. The merge\ntook #2004's smaller state stack and kept this branch's laws."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mutant"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Owner"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Result"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Retention kept"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"state-retention oracle"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"killed, 5 failures"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Held sync applies before the drop"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"state-retention oracle"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"killed, 12 failures"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isPersisted"},{"type":"text","value":" resolves before publication"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"state-retention oracle"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"killed, 44 failures"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Handler-facing receipt waits for visibility"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"state-retention oracle"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"killed, 5 failures"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Load settles at acceptance"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"load-subset oracle and state retention"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"killed, 11 and 4 failures"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"$origin"},{"type":"text","value":" marker persists until the next write"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"state-retention oracle"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"killed, 11 failures"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Held confirmation marked "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'remote'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"state-retention oracle"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"killed, 9 failures"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An open sync transaction counts for holds"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"state-retention oracle"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"killed, 5 failures"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Older held row wins over the newest completed row"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"state-retention oracle"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"killed, 1 failure"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pre-sync capture counts an open transaction"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"state-retention oracle"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"killed, 1 failure"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Replay invalidates a committed transaction instead of throwing"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"state-retention oracle"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"killed, 1 failure"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"DbClient chunk queues after open transactions"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"DbClient hydration oracle"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"killed, 2 failures"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Core abort listener drops an accepted transaction"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"load-subset and refinement oracles"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"killed, 1 and 1 failures"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Core abort listener calls the cancel path"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"load-subset and refinement oracles"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"survived; see below"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stale eager fetch applies"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Query Collection"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"killed"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Query cache reads applied rows"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Query Collection"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"killed"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Query Collection passes its signal to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"commit()"},{"type":"text","value":" again"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Query Collection"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"killed, 1 failure"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Query Collection rolls back accepted ownership on supersession"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ownership oracle"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"killed"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TrailBase aborted load resolves"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TrailBase"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"killed, 5 failures"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Electric aborted load resolves"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Electric"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"killed, 1 failure"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reject a source delete for a never-held key"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"state-retention oracle"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"killed, 11 failures"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Drop a source delete for a never-held key"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"state-retention oracle"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"survived; equivalent"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Corrections and survivors:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Signal passed to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"commit()"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"text","value":" the earlier run selected no test, because\nits name filter no longer matched the supersession test. With the correct\nfilter, the mutant fails. It is not equivalent, and the earlier note about\nit is withdrawn."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Dropped never-held delete:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" the key is absent from the applied synced\nrows, and the optimistic state drops at settlement either way. The\n"},{"type":"link","href":"2026-10-02-absent-key-source-delete.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"absent-key review"}]},{"type":"text","value":" records the\nrewritten pinned histories."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Core abort calls the cancel path:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cancelPendingSyncedTransaction"},{"type":"text","value":" now\nthrows "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SyncQueueInvariantError"},{"type":"text","value":" for a committed transaction. The guard\nstops the cancellation before it changes state, so the accepted rows still\napply. The unguarded variant, which removes the accepted transaction\ndirectly, fails in both oracles."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"limits","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Limits"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On-demand self-load:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" a handler that awaits an on-demand load of its own\nCollection waits for itself. This history is documented and outside the\ngenerated grammar."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Truncate:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" a truncate still applies while a transaction persists, and the\nstill-persisting transactions overlay it."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"duplicate subset loads correctly"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"text","value":" 0 of 10 full-file runs fail on\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"origin/main"},{"type":"text","value":". On the branch it failed every time because its handler wrote\nno confirmation, until the fixture was changed."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Eager refetch race:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" the guard covers eager mode. On-demand mode keeps its\npost-write authority path."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"verification","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Verification"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"At "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"3c85ac0de"},{"type":"text","value":" with built "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dist"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"db:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" 7920 tests, and 8224 with type checking; no type errors."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Query Collection:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" 945 tests with type checking; no type errors."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Other packages:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" Electric 629, persistence core 374, node SQLite 110,\nPowerSync 176, offline 242, TrailBase 67, RxDB 12. React, Vue, Solid, Svelte,\nand Angular pass."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Checks:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"test:oracles"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"check:mangle"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"test-minified-db"},{"type":"text","value":" pass."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"optimistic-state-drops-at-settlement","text":"Optimistic state drops at settlement","level":1},{"id":"law","text":"Law","level":2},{"id":"gap","text":"Gap","level":2},{"id":"repair-and-witnesses","text":"Repair and witnesses","level":2},{"id":"mutants","text":"Mutants","level":2},{"id":"after-the-merge-with-the-state-stack-refactor","text":"After the merge with the state-stack refactor","level":3},{"id":"limits","text":"Limits","level":2},{"id":"verification","text":"Verification","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"# Optimistic state drops at settlement\n\nPre-repair executable revision: `origin/main` at `95c3f9ec9`.\nRepair branch: `fix-settled-snapshot-ack`. Production code `b5e498ddb`\nthrough `9b82ac3dc`. Evidence head `3c85ac0de`.\n\n## Law\n\nAn optimistic transaction overlays its optimistic state only while its\nmutation function runs. When the mutation function settles, fulfilled or\nrejected, the state drops. Success does not wait for a sync confirmation: a\nhandler that returns before its server row arrives shows the previous synced\nrow until that row applies.\n\nA sync transaction committed while an optimistic transaction persists is\n*accepted* and held. It becomes *visible* in the publication that drops the\noptimistic state, and `isPersisted` settles after that publication.\n\nEach sync transaction therefore has two moments:\n\n- **Accepted:** `commit()` returns, or a persistence wrapper finishes its\n  durable step. Handler-facing writes wait for this moment: Query Collection\n  direct writes, persisted mutation confirmation and startup, and the PowerSync\n  mutation path.\n- **Visible:** the rows apply and publish. Commit receipts, subset loads, and\n  Collection readiness wait for this moment.\n\nAn accepted transaction always applies, in commit order, and a later abort\ncannot withdraw its rows. A load whose caller aborted still rejects with\n`AbortError`. A source discards a stale page by checking the signal before\n`commit()`.\n\nA sync write is `$origin: 'local'` only if it was committed while the\ntransaction persisted. A write committed after settlement is `'remote'`.\n\nAuthority: user decisions recorded in the PR discussion for this branch. These\nreplace the accepted-snapshot retention law (#1213, #1807, #1822, #1870) and\n`begin({ immediate })` (#1130).\n\n## Gap\n\nSince #1213, `recomputeOptimisticState` retained a completed direct\ntransaction's row until a later sync transaction wrote its key. Query\nCollection direct writes used `begin({ immediate: true })` to apply during\npersistence. After such a write, no later sync transaction retired the\nretained row. Passing runs of `awaits persisted server responses in update\nhandlers` depended on an unrelated persisted sync transaction arriving later.\n\nThe optimistic-history oracle encoded the retention law as its reference\nmodel, so the oracle agreed with the drift.\n\nIn #1990, a refetch canceled an earlier result's commit that was waiting for\nstorage. The cancellation invalidated the dependent result, and the collection\nentered `error`.\n\n## Repair and witnesses\n\n- **Core:** removes `begin({ immediate })`, post-commit cancellation, retention\n  and its dependency machinery, the truncate optimistic snapshot, and the\n  direct-transaction marker. The only hold left keeps a completed row while a\n  queued sync transaction touches its key.\n- **Receipts:** a commit receipt resolves at visibility. It carries its\n  acceptance moment (`withAcceptedReceipt` / `whenSyncAccepted`). Readiness\n  waits for accepted rows to publish.\n- **Query Collection:** direct writes read and validate accepted rows, and\n  update the Query cache after acceptance. That cache read was the root cause\n  of #1130. A refetch commits without a signal and no longer rolls back\n  accepted ownership. An eager fetch that started before a direct write is\n  discarded.\n- **Persistence:** stores a held source transaction at acceptance. Internal\n  applies inside the apply mutex wait only for acceptance. Electric reserves\n  its commit turn through `persistence.reserveCommitTurn()`.\n- **Electric and TrailBase:** reject an aborted load after its accepted rows\n  apply.\n- **Optimistic-history oracle:** the prose, model, grammar, and driver are\n  rewritten. The handler writes at every cut, with and without awaiting\n  acceptance. It observes the rows visible when `isPersisted` settles, allows a\n  single cut at settlement, keeps receipts pending while queued, and checks\n  `$origin` for held and later confirmations.\n\n| Run | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| #1990 refetch, first durable write held, on `origin/main` | 3 of 3 isolated runs fail: `expected 'error' to be 'ready'` |\n| #1990 handler `writeUpsert`, result write held, on `origin/main` | 4 of 5 full-file runs fail: `expected +0 to be 3` (the retained optimistic row) |\n| Real-SQLite handler test ported from #2002, on `origin/main` (`await source.commit()`) | times out after 5000 ms |\n| Same three on the branch | pass; Query Collection file passes 5 of 5 full-file runs |\n| `awaits persisted server responses in update handlers`, branch | 20 of 20 full-file runs pass |\n| Eager refetch older than a handler `writeUpsert`, before its fix | `expected 2 to be 3` |\n\n## Mutants\n\nEach mutant is a temporary production edit that is restored after its run.\n\n| Mutant | Owner | Result |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Retention kept: hold a completed row without a queued sync transaction | state-retention oracle | killed |\n| Held sync applies before the drop (immediate bypass) | state-retention oracle | killed, 11 failures |\n| `isPersisted` resolves before publication | state-retention oracle | killed, 40 failures |\n| Handler-facing receipt waits for visibility | state-retention oracle | killed, 6 failures |\n| Load settles at acceptance | load-subset oracle and state retention | killed, 10 and 4 failures |\n| `$origin` marker persists until the next write | state-retention oracle | killed, 6 failures |\n| Held confirmation marked `'remote'` | state-retention oracle | killed, 7 failures |\n| Core abort cancels an accepted transaction | load-subset and refinement oracles | killed |\n| Stale eager fetch applies | Query Collection | killed |\n| Query cache reads applied rows | Query Collection | killed |\n| TrailBase aborted load resolves | TrailBase | killed |\n| Electric aborted load resolves | Electric | killed |\n| Query Collection passes its signal to `commit()` again | Query Collection | survived; equivalent |\n| Query Collection rolls back accepted ownership on supersession | ownership oracle | survived at first, then killed |\n\nSurvivors:\n\n- **Signal passed to `commit()`:** this mutant is equivalent. Core now ignores\n  a post-commit abort, so the signal cannot cancel an accepted transaction. The\n  core-level mutant above covers this law.\n- **Ownership rollback:** every supersession test held durable storage. In that\n  case the result's core transaction had already applied, so restoring the old\n  ownership did nothing. The ownership oracle now also holds the result behind\n  a persisting mutation and checks visible and synced rows after each refetch,\n  including a later empty refetch. The mutant fails there.\n\n### After the merge with the state-stack refactor\n\nEvery mutant above, plus five more, ran again on the merged code. The merge\ntook #2004's smaller state stack and kept this branch's laws.\n\n| Mutant | Owner | Result |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Retention kept | state-retention oracle | killed, 5 failures |\n| Held sync applies before the drop | state-retention oracle | killed, 12 failures |\n| `isPersisted` resolves before publication | state-retention oracle | killed, 44 failures |\n| Handler-facing receipt waits for visibility | state-retention oracle | killed, 5 failures |\n| Load settles at acceptance | load-subset oracle and state retention | killed, 11 and 4 failures |\n| `$origin` marker persists until the next write | state-retention oracle | killed, 11 failures |\n| Held confirmation marked `'remote'` | state-retention oracle | killed, 9 failures |\n| An open sync transaction counts for holds | state-retention oracle | killed, 5 failures |\n| Older held row wins over the newest completed row | state-retention oracle | killed, 1 failure |\n| Pre-sync capture counts an open transaction | state-retention oracle | killed, 1 failure |\n| Replay invalidates a committed transaction instead of throwing | state-retention oracle | killed, 1 failure |\n| DbClient chunk queues after open transactions | DbClient hydration oracle | killed, 2 failures |\n| Core abort listener drops an accepted transaction | load-subset and refinement oracles | killed, 1 and 1 failures |\n| Core abort listener calls the cancel path | load-subset and refinement oracles | survived; see below |\n| Stale eager fetch applies | Query Collection | killed |\n| Query cache reads applied rows | Query Collection | killed |\n| Query Collection passes its signal to `commit()` again | Query Collection | killed, 1 failure |\n| Query Collection rolls back accepted ownership on supersession | ownership oracle | killed |\n| TrailBase aborted load resolves | TrailBase | killed, 5 failures |\n| Electric aborted load resolves | Electric | killed, 1 failure |\n| Reject a source delete for a never-held key | state-retention oracle | killed, 11 failures |\n| Drop a source delete for a never-held key | state-retention oracle | survived; equivalent |\n\nCorrections and survivors:\n\n- **Signal passed to `commit()`:** the earlier run selected no test, because\n  its name filter no longer matched the supersession test. With the correct\n  filter, the mutant fails. It is not equivalent, and the earlier note about\n  it is withdrawn.\n- **Dropped never-held delete:** the key is absent from the applied synced\n  rows, and the optimistic state drops at settlement either way. The\n  [absent-key review](2026-10-02-absent-key-source-delete.md) records the\n  rewritten pinned histories.\n- **Core abort calls the cancel path:** `cancelPendingSyncedTransaction` now\n  throws `SyncQueueInvariantError` for a committed transaction. The guard\n  stops the cancellation before it changes state, so the accepted rows still\n  apply. The unguarded variant, which removes the accepted transaction\n  directly, fails in both oracles.\n\n## Limits\n\n- **On-demand self-load:** a handler that awaits an on-demand load of its own\n  Collection waits for itself. This history is documented and outside the\n  generated grammar.\n- **Truncate:** a truncate still applies while a transaction persists, and the\n  still-persisting transactions overlay it.\n- **`duplicate subset loads correctly`:** 0 of 10 full-file runs fail on\n  `origin/main`. On the branch it failed every time because its handler wrote\n  no confirmation, until the fixture was changed.\n- **Eager refetch race:** the guard covers eager mode. On-demand mode keeps its\n  post-write authority path.\n\n## Verification\n\nAt `3c85ac0de` with built `dist`:\n\n- **db:** 7920 tests, and 8224 with type checking; no type errors.\n- **Query Collection:** 945 tests with type checking; no type errors.\n- **Other packages:** Electric 629, persistence core 374, node SQLite 110,\n  PowerSync 176, offline 242, TrailBase 67, RxDB 12. React, Vue, Solid, Svelte,\n  and Angular pass.\n- **Checks:** `test:oracles`, `check:mangle`, and `test-minified-db` pass.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"# Optimistic state drops at settlement\n\nPre-repair executable revision: `origin/main` at `95c3f9ec9`.\nRepair branch: `fix-settled-snapshot-ack`. Production code `b5e498ddb`\nthrough `9b82ac3dc`. Evidence head `3c85ac0de`.\n\n## Law\n\nAn optimistic transaction overlays its optimistic state only while its\nmutation function runs. When the mutation function settles, fulfilled or\nrejected, the state drops. Success does not wait for a sync confirmation: a\nhandler that returns before its server row arrives shows the previous synced\nrow until that row applies.\n\nA sync transaction committed while an optimistic transaction persists is\n*accepted* and held. It becomes *visible* in the publication that drops the\noptimistic state, and `isPersisted` settles after that publication.\n\nEach sync transaction therefore has two moments:\n\n- **Accepted:** `commit()` returns, or a persistence wrapper finishes its\n  durable step. Handler-facing writes wait for this moment: Query Collection\n  direct writes, persisted mutation confirmation and startup, and the PowerSync\n  mutation path.\n- **Visible:** the rows apply and publish. Commit receipts, subset loads, and\n  Collection readiness wait for this moment.\n\nAn accepted transaction always applies, in commit order, and a later abort\ncannot withdraw its rows. A load whose caller aborted still rejects with\n`AbortError`. A source discards a stale page by checking the signal before\n`commit()`.\n\nA sync write is `$origin: 'local'` only if it was committed while the\ntransaction persisted. A write committed after settlement is `'remote'`.\n\nAuthority: user decisions recorded in the PR discussion for this branch. These\nreplace the accepted-snapshot retention law (#1213, #1807, #1822, #1870) and\n`begin({ immediate })` (#1130).\n\n## Gap\n\nSince #1213, `recomputeOptimisticState` retained a completed direct\ntransaction's row until a later sync transaction wrote its key. Query\nCollection direct writes used `begin({ immediate: true })` to apply during\npersistence. After such a write, no later sync transaction retired the\nretained row. Passing runs of `awaits persisted server responses in update\nhandlers` depended on an unrelated persisted sync transaction arriving later.\n\nThe optimistic-history oracle encoded the retention law as its reference\nmodel, so the oracle agreed with the drift.\n\nIn #1990, a refetch canceled an earlier result's commit that was waiting for\nstorage. The cancellation invalidated the dependent result, and the collection\nentered `error`.\n\n## Repair and witnesses\n\n- **Core:** removes `begin({ immediate })`, post-commit cancellation, retention\n  and its dependency machinery, the truncate optimistic snapshot, and the\n  direct-transaction marker. The only hold left keeps a completed row while a\n  queued sync transaction touches its key.\n- **Receipts:** a commit receipt resolves at visibility. It carries its\n  acceptance moment (`withAcceptedReceipt` / `whenSyncAccepted`). Readiness\n  waits for accepted rows to publish.\n- **Query Collection:** direct writes read and validate accepted rows, and\n  update the Query cache after acceptance. That cache read was the root cause\n  of #1130. A refetch commits without a signal and no longer rolls back\n  accepted ownership. An eager fetch that started before a direct write is\n  discarded.\n- **Persistence:** stores a held source transaction at acceptance. Internal\n  applies inside the apply mutex wait only for acceptance. Electric reserves\n  its commit turn through `persistence.reserveCommitTurn()`.\n- **Electric and TrailBase:** reject an aborted load after its accepted rows\n  apply.\n- **Optimistic-history oracle:** the prose, model, grammar, and driver are\n  rewritten. The handler writes at every cut, with and without awaiting\n  acceptance. It observes the rows visible when `isPersisted` settles, allows a\n  single cut at settlement, keeps receipts pending while queued, and checks\n  `$origin` for held and later confirmations.\n\n| Run | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| #1990 refetch, first durable write held, on `origin/main` | 3 of 3 isolated runs fail: `expected 'error' to be 'ready'` |\n| #1990 handler `writeUpsert`, result write held, on `origin/main` | 4 of 5 full-file runs fail: `expected +0 to be 3` (the retained optimistic row) |\n| Real-SQLite handler test ported from #2002, on `origin/main` (`await source.commit()`) | times out after 5000 ms |\n| Same three on the branch | pass; Query Collection file passes 5 of 5 full-file runs |\n| `awaits persisted server responses in update handlers`, branch | 20 of 20 full-file runs pass |\n| Eager refetch older than a handler `writeUpsert`, before its fix | `expected 2 to be 3` |\n\n## Mutants\n\nEach mutant is a temporary production edit that is restored after its run.\n\n| Mutant | Owner | Result |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Retention kept: hold a completed row without a queued sync transaction | state-retention oracle | killed |\n| Held sync applies before the drop (immediate bypass) | state-retention oracle | killed, 11 failures |\n| `isPersisted` resolves before publication | state-retention oracle | killed, 40 failures |\n| Handler-facing receipt waits for visibility | state-retention oracle | killed, 6 failures |\n| Load settles at acceptance | load-subset oracle and state retention | killed, 10 and 4 failures |\n| `$origin` marker persists until the next write | state-retention oracle | killed, 6 failures |\n| Held confirmation marked `'remote'` | state-retention oracle | killed, 7 failures |\n| Core abort cancels an accepted transaction | load-subset and refinement oracles | killed |\n| Stale eager fetch applies | Query Collection | killed |\n| Query cache reads applied rows | Query Collection | killed |\n| TrailBase aborted load resolves | TrailBase | killed |\n| Electric aborted load resolves | Electric | killed |\n| Query Collection passes its signal to `commit()` again | Query Collection | survived; equivalent |\n| Query Collection rolls back accepted ownership on supersession | ownership oracle | survived at first, then killed |\n\nSurvivors:\n\n- **Signal passed to `commit()`:** this mutant is equivalent. Core now ignores\n  a post-commit abort, so the signal cannot cancel an accepted transaction. The\n  core-level mutant above covers this law.\n- **Ownership rollback:** every supersession test held durable storage. In that\n  case the result's core transaction had already applied, so restoring the old\n  ownership did nothing. The ownership oracle now also holds the result behind\n  a persisting mutation and checks visible and synced rows after each refetch,\n  including a later empty refetch. The mutant fails there.\n\n### After the merge with the state-stack refactor\n\nEvery mutant above, plus five more, ran again on the merged code. The merge\ntook #2004's smaller state stack and kept this branch's laws.\n\n| Mutant | Owner | Result |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Retention kept | state-retention oracle | killed, 5 failures |\n| Held sync applies before the drop | state-retention oracle | killed, 12 failures |\n| `isPersisted` resolves before publication | state-retention oracle | killed, 44 failures |\n| Handler-facing receipt waits for visibility | state-retention oracle | killed, 5 failures |\n| Load settles at acceptance | load-subset oracle and state retention | killed, 11 and 4 failures |\n| `$origin` marker persists until the next write | state-retention oracle | killed, 11 failures |\n| Held confirmation marked `'remote'` | state-retention oracle | killed, 9 failures |\n| An open sync transaction counts for holds | state-retention oracle | killed, 5 failures |\n| Older held row wins over the newest completed row | state-retention oracle | killed, 1 failure |\n| Pre-sync capture counts an open transaction | state-retention oracle | killed, 1 failure |\n| Replay invalidates a committed transaction instead of throwing | state-retention oracle | killed, 1 failure |\n| DbClient chunk queues after open transactions | DbClient hydration oracle | killed, 2 failures |\n| Core abort listener drops an accepted transaction | load-subset and refinement oracles | killed, 1 and 1 failures |\n| Core abort listener calls the cancel path | load-subset and refinement oracles | survived; see below |\n| Stale eager fetch applies | Query Collection | killed |\n| Query cache reads applied rows | Query Collection | killed |\n| Query Collection passes its signal to `commit()` again | Query Collection | killed, 1 failure |\n| Query Collection rolls back accepted ownership on supersession | ownership oracle | killed |\n| TrailBase aborted load resolves | TrailBase | killed, 5 failures |\n| Electric aborted load resolves | Electric | killed, 1 failure |\n| Reject a source delete for a never-held key | state-retention oracle | killed, 11 failures |\n| Drop a source delete for a never-held key | state-retention oracle | survived; equivalent |\n\nCorrections and survivors:\n\n- **Signal passed to `commit()`:** the earlier run selected no test, because\n  its name filter no longer matched the supersession test. With the correct\n  filter, the mutant fails. It is not equivalent, and the earlier note about\n  it is withdrawn.\n- **Dropped never-held delete:** the key is absent from the applied synced\n  rows, and the optimistic state drops at settlement either way. The\n  [absent-key review](2026-10-02-absent-key-source-delete.md) records the\n  rewritten pinned histories.\n- **Core abort calls the cancel path:** `cancelPendingSyncedTransaction` now\n  throws `SyncQueueInvariantError` for a committed transaction. The guard\n  stops the cancellation before it changes state, so the accepted rows still\n  apply. The unguarded variant, which removes the accepted transaction\n  directly, fails in both oracles.\n\n## Limits\n\n- **On-demand self-load:** a handler that awaits an on-demand load of its own\n  Collection waits for itself. This history is documented and outside the\n  generated grammar.\n- **Truncate:** a truncate still applies while a transaction persists, and the\n  still-persisting transactions overlay it.\n- **`duplicate subset loads correctly`:** 0 of 10 full-file runs fail on\n  `origin/main`. On the branch it failed every time because its handler wrote\n  no confirmation, until the fixture was changed.\n- **Eager refetch race:** the guard covers eager mode. On-demand mode keeps its\n  post-write authority path.\n\n## Verification\n\nAt `3c85ac0de` with built `dist`:\n\n- **db:** 7920 tests, and 8224 with type checking; no type errors.\n- **Query Collection:** 945 tests with type checking; no type errors.\n- **Other packages:** Electric 629, persistence core 374, node SQLite 110,\n  PowerSync 176, offline 242, TrailBase 67, RxDB 12. React, Vue, Solid, Svelte,\n  and Angular pass.\n- **Checks:** `test:oracles`, `check:mangle`, and `test-minified-db` pass.\n"}
